{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 473143, "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "username": "darthziplock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-20T03:28:39.580Z", "cooked": "<p>Fedora 43 KDE. Title says all. Just a week after solving the problem of Baloo burning my CPU and thrashing my drive, now I’ve got these localsearch-3 and localsearch-extractor-3 processes that randomly pop up, eat my CPU, and refuse to be killed.</p>\n<p>I send the “kill” signal via System Monitor, and they pop right back up instantly, still burning away. Only a reboot gets them to go away, but they always come back in a day or two.</p>\n<p>And it’s not like they’re building an index either. I’ve let them go for over 24 hours, hoping they’ll finish up, but they never do.</p>\n<p>Given that these seem to be Gnome-related file search processes, how do I block them from running? I’ve disabled Baloo by turning off Indexing via System Settings, but I’m not finding any answers on how to keep these processes from eating my CPU alive.</p>\n<p>Help please!</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-20T03:28:39.580Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2325, "reads": 36, "readers_count": 35, "score": 11502.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Taylor Rhodes", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28821, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473161, "name": "MatH", "username": "theprogram", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/theprogram/{size}/53169_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-20T06:25:53.979Z", "cooked": "<p>have you tried removing them with dnf remove ?</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-20T06:25:53.979Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 8, "reads": 35, "readers_count": 34, "score": 52.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "MatH", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": "mindshare", "flair_url": "book-atlas", "flair_bg_color": "51a2daff", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 63, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Welcome Wagon", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16174, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473293, "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "username": "darthziplock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-20T18:05:52.205Z", "cooked": "<p>$ sudo dnf search installed localsearch* keeps telling me no matches found. Doesn’t even return results when using the exact name of the process. Must be a part of a larger package.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-20T18:05:52.205Z", "reply_count": 2, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 31, "readers_count": 30, "score": 46.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Taylor Rhodes", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 16174, "username": "theprogram", "name": "MatH", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/theprogram/{size}/53169_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28821, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473315, "name": "MatH", "username": "theprogram", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/theprogram/{size}/53169_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-20T19:19:18.048Z", "cooked": "<p>Find the pid of the problematic processes, with something like top btop or ps and then find their parent processes ppid with ps -ef</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://fedoramagazine.org/inspect-manage-processes-ps/\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/d/d/ddcb24a05f263ad2ed61e4204da1643841476f0d.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"5078B2\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://fedoramagazine.org/inspect-manage-processes-ps/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"08:00AM - 09 February 2018\">Fedora Magazine – 9 Feb 18</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/291;\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/b/7/b7a8f0a4b5577fa77c07fc7e176125ba3debf022_2_690x292.jpeg\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"777968\" width=\"690\" height=\"292\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://fedoramagazine.org/inspect-manage-processes-ps/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Inspect and manage processes with ps - Fedora Magazine</a></h3>\n\n  <p>Learn how to use the ps command line utility to gain insight into the processes running on your Fedora system in this Magazine article.</p>\n\n  <p>\n    <span class=\"label1\">Est. reading time: 6 minutes</span>\n  </p>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>If you eventually fimd that its a KDE function, then you will have trouble removing it.  If you somehow got infected with Gnome, removal should be possible.</p>\n<p>And have a look at <a href=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/fedora/f40/system-administrators-guide/monitoring-and-automation/System_Monitoring_Tools/#s2-sysinfo-system-processes-system_monitor\">system monitor</a> tool, it should be able to show you a dependency tree</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-20T19:21:42.148Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 13, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 71.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "MatH", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": "mindshare", "flair_url": "book-atlas", "flair_bg_color": "51a2daff", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 63, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/fedora/f40/system-administrators-guide/monitoring-and-automation/System_Monitoring_Tools/#s2-sysinfo-system-processes-system_monitor", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 5}, {"url": "https://fedoramagazine.org/inspect-manage-processes-ps/", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Inspect and manage processes with ps - Fedora Magazine", "clicks": 3}], "read": true, "user_title": "Welcome Wagon", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 28821, "username": "darthziplock", "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16174, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473370, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-21T02:50:40.085Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"darthziplock\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"179794\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Taylor Rhodes:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>sudo dnf search installed localsearch*</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><code>sudo dnf list --installed localsearch*</code></p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-21T02:50:40.085Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 46, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 240.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 28821, "username": "darthziplock", "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473378, "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "username": "darthziplock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-21T03:57:55.038Z", "cooked": "<p>Oh duh. Output:</p>\n<p>Installed packages<br>\nlocalsearch.x86_64 3.10.2-1.fc43 </p>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/theprogram\">@theprogram</a> mentioned somehow getting infected with Gnome, and I think that’s what happened. The Music app I was trying turns out to be Gnome’s music app, and that’s about when the localsearch issues started.</p>\n<p>I still hesitate to sudo dnf remove localsearch* cuz there are a few things in there and I don’t want something else to break:</p>\n<p>Package                                    Arch        Version                                    Repository                 Size<br>\nRemoving:<br>\nlocalsearch                               x86_64      3.10.2-1.fc43                                             3.4 MiB<br>\nRemoving unused dependencies:<br>\nexempi                                    x86_64      2.6.4-8.fc43                                              1.4 MiB<br>\nlibcue                                    x86_64      2.3.0-12.fc43                                            85.8 KiB<br>\nlibgsf                                    x86_64      1.14.54-1.fc43                                          964.9 KiB<br>\nlibgxps                                   x86_64      0.3.2-11.fc43                                           188.1 KiB<br>\nlibiptcdata                               x86_64      1.0.5-23.fc43                                           163.9 KiB<br>\nlibosinfo                                 x86_64      1.12.0-3.fc43                                             1.2 MiB<br>\nosinfo-db                                 noarch      20250124-2.fc43                                           3.9 MiB<br>\nosinfo-db-tools                           x86_64      1.12.0-4.fc43                                           190.9 KiB<br>\npoppler-glib                              x86_64      25.07.0-3.fc43                                          633.9 KiB<br>\ntotem-pl-parser                           x86_64      3.26.6-13.fc43                                          308.5 KiB<br>\nuchardet                                  x86_64      0.0.8-8.fc43                                            275.6 KiB</p>\n<p>Transaction Summary:<br>\nRemoving:          12 packages</p>\n<p>After this operation, 13 MiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 13 MiB).</p>\n<p>Is there a dnf command to see what might depend on localsearch?</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-21T04:00:21.602Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 33, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 185.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Taylor Rhodes", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 638, "username": "grumpey", "name": "Joe Walker", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28821, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 16174, "username": "theprogram", "name": "MatH", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/theprogram/{size}/53169_2.png"}], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 473383, "name": "MatH", "username": "theprogram", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/theprogram/{size}/53169_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-21T06:38:38.721Z", "cooked": "<p>those packages you listed are what will be removed.</p>\n<p>If you also try removing totem, you should get the same list.</p>\n<p>You can remove those files, if needed you can put them back.</p>\n<p>For a music player, I use rhythmbox</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-21T06:38:38.721Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 42, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 215.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "MatH", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": "mindshare", "flair_url": "book-atlas", "flair_bg_color": "51a2daff", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 63, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Welcome Wagon", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 28821, "username": "darthziplock", "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16174, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 474197, "name": "Vanadium", "username": "ytrium", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/y/51a2da/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-25T11:47:15.016Z", "cooked": "<p>I systematically used to disable tracker, but nowadays, I have good experience disabling all file content searches. In Search (Settings), under “Search Locations”, disable everything. This should stop the “mining”  of files (for metadata and contents), but still keep file name search in Files snappy.</p>\n<p>Then it may be good to clean out the database: it may be corrupt in your case. I see no other way than</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Log out of your account</li>\n<li>Log in on a virtual console, and delete the cache files: <code>rm -rf ~/.cache/tracker3</code> (the old name remained here).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>When you log back in, a new database will be created, but as you are not mining files, it will remain small (9.3 M on my system).</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-01-25T11:47:15.016Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 76, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 394.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Vanadium", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 7746, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/8", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 497287, "name": "Taylor Rhodes", "username": "darthziplock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-04-26T16:40:52.203Z", "cooked": "<p>Well I reinstalled my Fedora system, but this time using Workstation, and now localsearch-3 is burning my PC up again. Always sitting at exactly 12.5% CPU usage and immediately comes back after being force-quit.</p>", "post_number": 9, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-04-26T16:40:52.203Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 30, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 153.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Taylor Rhodes", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28821, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/9", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 517455, "name": "Hemant Kumar Meena", "username": "hemu312", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/h/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-07-16T11:09:39.232Z", "cooked": "<p>Guys, I used this trick to solve heavy resource usage by it. BTW I also don’t like some program to look inside my files without my permission.<br>\ngsettings set org.freedesktop.Tracker3.Extract max-bytes 0<br>\nThis tricks it into indexing only filenames.<br>\ngsettings set org.freedesktop.Tracker3.Extract text-allowlist “[]”<br>\ndisable text extraction</p>\n<p>Now search also works well without problems.</p>\n<p>Sorry for my formatting, I’m not good at that.</p>", "post_number": 10, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 10, "updated_at": "2026-07-16T11:10:12.589Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 28, "reads": 12, "readers_count": 11, "score": 157.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179794, "topic_slug": "localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed", "display_username": "Hemant Kumar Meena", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 17901, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/localsearch-3-and-localsearch-extractor-3-processes-taking-cpu-and-refuse-to-be-killed/179794/10", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [473143, 473161, 473293, 473315, 473370, 473378, 473383, 474197, 497287, 517455]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 288], [5, 287], [8, 283], [9, 192], [10, 111]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 395, "name": "kde", "slug": "kde"}, {"id": 1315, "name": "f43", "slug": "f43"}], "tags_descriptions": {}, "fancy_title": "Localsearch-3 and localsearch-extractor-3 processes taking CPU and refuse to be killed", "id": 179794, "title": "Localsearch-3 and localsearch-extractor-3 processes taking CPU and refuse to be killed", "posts_count": 10, "created_at": "2026-01-20T03:28:39.505Z", "views": 2349, "reply_count": 5, "like_count": 3